WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
From a public dataset to a shareable map story, in a few minutes.

2
00:00:06.543 --> 00:00:12.853
Everything in Vizzie lives in a project: the map, the charts, and the story you tell with them.

3
00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:26.843
Start with a place. Vizzie finds the government portals that publish data about it.

4
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:45.280
Quick maps put parcels, zoning and census a click away. To go further, search every portal at once, or pick one you trust. Here, the State of California's open data portal.

5
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:53.113
Search for the housing element progress reports. Results are datasets, and opening one goes straight to its preview.

6
00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:07.970
This is every housing application California's cities and counties reported: 358,000 rows. Too many to load at once.

7
00:01:08.472 --> 00:01:17.352
Narrow it to Los Angeles County in 2025, and it fits. Each application carries coordinates, so every one can go on the map.

8
00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.340
One click on Viz it gives you a first draft: the map and its legend.

9
00:01:32.684 --> 00:01:44.064
Open the layer to restyle it. Weight the density by proposed homes rather than applications, so a large apartment building counts for more than a backyard cottage.

10
00:01:50.988 --> 00:01:59.878
Add the same data again as points, coloured by type. Blue is accessory dwelling units: two in every three applications.

11
00:02:32.142 --> 00:02:39.352
The basemap can change too. Switch to satellite imagery, and the same data sits over the real landscape.

12
00:02:48.129 --> 00:02:54.829
Pick the columns you care about, and charts are offered as answers to questions, each with a live preview.

13
00:03:10.717 --> 00:03:15.437
Filter the charts to the map view, and they re-rank for the place you're looking at.

14
00:03:26.324 --> 00:03:32.544
Sketch layers let you mark up exactly what you want people to see. They stay pinned to the map as you zoom.

15
00:04:06.488 --> 00:04:14.788
A frame saves the view, the layers that are on, the charts, and the legend. Put frames in order, and you have a story.

16
00:04:53.027 --> 00:04:56.477
Present turns your frames into a slideshow.

17
00:05:07.371 --> 00:05:15.671
Publish it as an interactive presentation. Anyone with the link can open it, with no account, and the data credit stays attached.

18
00:05:30.811 --> 00:05:34.571
Vizzie. Free during beta, at vizzie.org.
